  RAW line BER, no framer -- the PHY on its own, so the two codes are
  compared without the protocol amplifying a small error (below).
  AMI `gain` is the receive amplitude error spec.md 5 rejected it for.

  code                         0.0       0.4       0.5       0.6       0.7
  biphase                       ok        ok        ok        ok   9.4e-05
  ami, exact amplitude          ok   4.7e-05   3.0e-04   3.0e-03   1.1e-02
  ami, 0.8x amplitude           ok        ok   6.3e-05   6.3e-04   2.7e-03
  ami, 0.6x amplitude           ok   3.4e-04   2.1e-03   6.1e-03   1.3e-02

  Biphase decides on transition TIMING against a 0.75-cell monostable,
  so noise must displace an edge by a quarter cell to cause an error.
  AMI decides on AMPLITUDE against a threshold at half the received
  peak, and at equal peak line voltage that is the smaller margin --
  which is why AMI loses here despite half the noise bandwidth.

