           0     8.34     +0.00         0    0.10%         999 ms
           1     8.34     +0.00         0    0.10%         999 ms
          10     6.23     -2.35         5    0.68%         475 ms
         100 too short         -        65    7.91%          71 ms
        1000  no lock         -       272   51.82%           0 ms

  Impulse noise costs BOTH continuity and fidelity, and the cliff is
  between 1 and 10 events/s:
    1/s     carrier exactly transparent, +0.00 dB, no breaks
    10/s    5 reframes/s AND -2.35 dB within the unbroken stretches --
            impulses that never unseat the framer still corrupt bits
    100/s   longest unbroken stretch 71 ms; no usable audio
    1000/s  the framer never locks at all
  Each reframe is a mute (spec.md 10), so the audible result at 10/s is
  five dropouts a second over speech that is already 2.3 dB degraded.


