MITIGATION -- the dead time is already in the receiver
  spec.md 6.1 ignores transitions within 0.2 cell of the last accepted
  one; rx_review.py measures 0.05-0.30 usable.  Bits lost at 200/s,
  amplitude 1.5, 2 seeds:

      dead            bits lost
      0.05         [1622, 1755]
      0.15         [1627, 1760]
      0.25         [1665, 1820]
      0.35         [2239, 2418]
      0.45         [3789, 4135]

  Dead time rejects edges that arrive too EARLY.  A stuck comparator
  removes edges instead, so there is nothing for it to reject: it is
  the wrong tool for this failure and does not help.

IMPULSE SUSCEPTIBILITY -- AMI, the same test as 10
  AMI decides |x| > thresh*peak.  An offset of ~0.5 either fakes a mark
